 "q2_10q_debt_note": {
  "filed": "2026-08-10",
  "source": "Marlowe Clinical Diagnostics Holdings, Inc. Form 10-Q for the quarter ended June 30, 2026, Note 8 (Debt), excerpt",
  "excerpt": "The Credit Agreement requires the Company to maintain a maximum Total Net Leverage Ratio of 5.00 to 1.00, tested quarterly. As of June 30, 2026, the Company's Total Net Leverage Ratio was 5.62 to 1.00, and the Company was therefore not in compliance with this covenant, which constitutes an Event of Default under the Credit Agreement (the 'Specified Default'). On August 7, 2026, the Company entered into a Forbearance Agreement with the Administrative Agent, lenders holding approximately 78% of the outstanding term loans and all of the revolving lenders. Under the Forbearance Agreement, the consenting lenders agreed to forbear from exercising their rights and remedies, including acceleration, with respect to the Specified Default until the earlier of September 4, 2026 and the occurrence of specified termination events. The Forbearance Agreement does not waive the Specified Default. During the forbearance period the Company may not request additional revolving loans. Because the forbearance is temporary, the Company's term loans of $410.0 million have been classified as current liabilities as of June 30, 2026."
 },
 "form_8k_amendment": {
  "filed": "2026-08-27",
  "items": [
   "1.01",
   "9.01"
  ],
  "excerpt": "On August 25, 2026, Marlowe Clinical Diagnostics Holdings, Inc. (the 'Company') entered into Amendment No. 4 and Limited Waiver to Credit Agreement (the 'Amendment') with Ashbury National Bank, N.A., as administrative agent, and the lenders party thereto constituting the Required Lenders and all Revolving Lenders. Pursuant to the Amendment: (i) the lenders waived the Event of Default arising from the Company's failure to comply with the maximum Total Net Leverage Ratio for the fiscal quarter ended June 30, 2026; (ii) the Total Net Leverage Ratio covenant will not be tested for the fiscal quarter ending September 30, 2026; (iii) the maximum Total Net Leverage Ratio will be 6.25 to 1.00 for the fiscal quarter ending December 31, 2026, 5.75 to 1.00 for the fiscal quarter ending March 31, 2027 and 5.00 to 1.00 for each fiscal quarter thereafter; (iv) the Company must maintain Liquidity of not less than $20.0 million, tested as of the last day of each calendar month beginning September 30, 2026, where 'Liquidity' means unrestricted cash and cash equivalents plus unused revolving commitments available to be borrowed (revolving commitments less outstanding revolving loans and letters of credit); (v) the applicable margin on the term loans increased by 1.50% per annum, of which 1.00% per annum will be paid in kind; (vi) the aggregate revolving commitments were reduced from $75.0 million to $60.0 million; and (vii) Ridgefield Capital Partners, the Company's majority stockholder, contributed $30.0 million in cash as common equity, of which $25.0 million was applied to prepay term loans. The Amendment provides that this contribution does not constitute a 'Cure Amount' under Section 8.03 of the Credit Agreement and shall not be included in Consolidated EBITDA for any purpose. The Forbearance Agreement dated August 7, 2026 terminated upon the effectiveness of the Amendment. The Company paid consenting lenders an amendment fee equal to 0.50% of their term loans and revolving commitments."
